# SABOTAGE: issue #11 / EG6 — the chokepoint's usage scrub MERGES into the adapter's map
# instead of REBUILDING it, so any other key the adapter put in the usage slot (a "leak"
# key carrying the prompt, say) travels past the normalizer to the agent loop. The usage
# channel is the one place adapter-authored data now crosses the chokepoint; it must be
# narrower than the reason channel, never wider.
#
# Flips the extra-key test. The plain-usage test and the bad-count test stay green (the
# two counts are still right), which is why only an allowlist assertion catches it.
# Re-anchored for issue #74 (separate cached/uncached buckets): every billing site now
# goes through `spent/1` / `spend_attrs/2`, so the surrounding code moved. Same edit.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/chokepoint_error_usage_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: EG6: no other key in the usage map travels — the map is rebuilt, never passed through
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
index b4b9429..1a2267b 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/chokepoint.ex
@@ -411,11 +411,13 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Chokepoint do
   # (`:cached_input_tokens` is input served from the prompt cache, issue #74). Any other key, and any value
   # that is not a non-negative integer, is dropped (a bad value bills 0, never a guess).
   defp scrub_usage(usage) do
-    %{
+    # SABOTAGE (#11 / EG6): the adapter's map is MERGED into, not rebuilt — every other
+    # key it put in the usage slot now travels past the normalizer.
+    Map.merge(usage, %{
       input_tokens: usage_count(usage, :input_tokens),
       cached_input_tokens: usage_count(usage, :cached_input_tokens),
       output_tokens: usage_count(usage, :output_tokens)
-    }
+    })
   end
 
